CAT = "dkmcBike"; SEG = "BIK"
# Afsnit 1: the motorcycle, its equipment and documents, and personal protective gear.
Q = [
("On a Danish motorcycle, which brake must be worked by a lever on the right handlebar?",
 "The front brake", ["The rear brake", "The sidecar brake", "The parking brake"],
 "The front wheel brake must be hand-operated with its lever on the right side of the handlebar. The rear brake can be worked by foot or by hand and may be linked to the front."),
("In which situation is the engine kill switch (motorstop) meant to be used?",
 "When the bike has fallen over", ["Every time you park", "When waiting at red lights", "When riding downhill"],
 "The kill switch lets you stop the engine quickly if the motorcycle falls over or in a similar emergency. In normal use you switch off with the ignition."),
("Which braking system must a newer two-wheeled motorcycle have?",
 "ABS", ["A linked hand brake", "A sidecar brake", "A parking lock"],
 "Newer two-wheeled motorcycles must be fitted with ABS, which stops the wheels locking under braking. When ABS works, you feel it as vibration in the lever or pedal."),
("You squeeze the hydraulic front brake lever and hold it with steady force. It slowly creeps closer to the grip. What does this show?",
 "A fault in the brake system", ["Normal play in the lever", "Brake pads that are bedding in", "Brake fluid that is too cold"],
 "Under steady pressure a hydraulic lever or pedal must not sink. If it creeps towards the grip, there is a fault and the brakes must be checked at once."),
("What is the minimum tread depth in the main grooves of a motorcycle tyre in Denmark?",
 "1 mm", ["1.6 mm", "2 mm", "3 mm"],
 "A motorcycle tyre needs at least 1 mm in the main tread pattern, judged by the wear indicators if fitted. The 1.6 mm figure is the rule for cars."),
("You have just had brand-new tyres fitted. What should you bear in mind on the first ride?",
 "They can be very slippery", ["They grip best when cold", "They need extra air pressure", "They allow later braking"],
 "New tyres can be very smooth at first and call for especially careful riding until they have been run in."),
("Your bike stood in the garage for several seasons and the tyres still have deep tread. Why might they still be unsafe?",
 "Old rubber can harden", ["Tread depth always shrinks", "Old tyres lose their pressure", "The size marking fades"],
 "Tyres on a bike that rides little can grow old, hard or develop edges even when the tread is still legal, which makes the bike harder to handle."),
("Why can a chain that is too tight, too slack or badly worn be dangerous?",
 "It can jump off and lock the wheel", ["It can make the front brake fade", "It can drain the battery quickly", "It can bend the front forks"],
 "A chain in poor condition can jump off the sprockets and block the rear wheel. Keep it lubricated and adjusted to the maker's slack."),
("During a hard stop, the telescopic front forks bottom out with a thump. What does this indicate?",
 "A fault in the suspension", ["Correct fork adjustment", "Too much air in the tyres", "A heavy rider on board"],
 "Forks that bottom out under heavy braking are a sign of a fault. Working shock absorbers let the front rise and settle at once after being pressed down."),
("How far ahead must a motorcycle's main beam light up the road?",
 "At least 100 m", ["At least 30 m", "At least 50 m", "At least 300 m"],
 "The main beam on a motorcycle must light the road at least 100 m ahead. Dipped beam must reach at least 30 m without dazzling."),
("Which lights must a sidecar carry near its outer edge?",
 "White position light, red rear light", ["Two amber side lights only", "A white rear light and reflector", "A red front light only"],
 "A sidecar must have a white position light and a red rear light placed as near its outer edge as possible, plus a red rear reflector. On a two-wheeled motorcycle with sidecar, the right-hand indicators go on the sidecar."),
("Which mirrors must a newer solo motorcycle have?",
 "One on each side", ["One on the left only", "One on the right only", "None, a head check is enough"],
 "Motorcycles must have a rider's mirror on each side; only older motorcycles are exempt. A large moped needs only a left mirror."),
("Your windscreen is so tall that you look over it and cannot see the road 10 m ahead. What must it then have?",
 "A wiper and a washer", ["A tinted top edge", "A reflective strip", "A quick-release mount"],
 "A windscreen too high to see the roadway 10 m ahead over its top must be fitted with a wiper and washer. Any windscreen must be clear safety glass and firmly fixed."),
("Which marking shows that a helmet is approved for use in Denmark?",
 "A DS, FS, SS or E mark", ["A CE mark on the visor", "A manufacturer's logo", "A dealer's sales label"],
 "An approved crash helmet is DS, FS, SS or E marked and the right size. It may only be painted or have stickers added as the maker allows."),
("Why is riding with a backpack a risk for a motorcyclist?",
 "It can injure your back badly", ["It makes your helmet loosen", "It raises fuel use sharply", "It hides your rear number plate"],
 "A backpack can cause serious back injuries in a crash. A back protector does the opposite and can reduce back injuries."),
("You want to tow a small trailer with your motorcycle. What engine size must the bike have at least?",
 "125 cm³", ["50 cm³", "250 cm³", "500 cm³"],
 "A motorcycle used to tow a trailer must have a cylinder capacity of at least 125 cm³. The trailer may weigh at most 200 kg, laden, and must not carry people."),
]
